          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Chen-Ruan cohomology
            (
            %a{:href => "#ChenRuan00"}> Chen-Ruan 00
            ) of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            is the traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+cohomology"} orbifold cohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inertia+orbifold"} inertia orbifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \mathcal{X}
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+cohomology"} rational cohomology
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cohomology"} complex cohomology
            of the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quotient+space"} topological quotient space
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \mathcal{X}
          %p
            Chen-Ruan cohomology is motivated from the role that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            play as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spaces"} target spaces
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative string theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFTs"} 2d CFTs
